    "created_at": "2022-10-17T02:22:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-10-17T02:22:01Z",
    "body": "We discussed this in the triage meeting (#8250). There were not very strong feelings, but generally the room was against creating something as generic as this proposed Script header, instead favoring separate headers like `Speculation-Rules:` and `Import-Map:`.\r\n\r\nThere was also some discussion about how the `Link:` header has proven problematically over-generic in the past; some people thought there might be TAG guidance against such over-generic designs. (But, we weren't able to find any such TAG guidance when looking after the meeting.)\r\n\r\nFinally, in the most recent meeting @annevk pointed out that some WebKit folks were concerned about this general class of headers making pages less serializable, because the common serialization formats of today (namely: a `.html` file plus a folder of subresources; or, a `.mhtml` file) do not have room for expressing headers. This is an existing problem though, including stuff like `Content-Type` for charset declarations, CORP+COEP for capabilities, and the Firefox-only `Link:` with `rel=\"stylesheet\"`. I pointed out that newer serialiation formats such as [web bundles](https://wpack-wg.github.io/bundled-responses/draft-ietf-wpack-bundled-responses.html) solve this.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
